        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Downtown East, Minneapolis; Mill District; Minneapolis, Minnesota; University of Minnesota campus\n- Organizations: Minnesota Golden Gophers; University of Minnesota\n- Products: TCF Bank Stadium\n- People: Pat Westrum\n- Roles: professional ice hockey defenseman\n- Organizations: Minnesota Fighting Saints; Calgary Cowboys; Birmingham Bulls; World Hockey Association\n\nFacts:\n- Pat Westrum was born on March 3, 1948, in Minneapolis, Minnesota.\n- Pat Westrum is a retired professional ice hockey defenseman.\n- Between 1974 and 1978, Pat Westrum played 237 regular season games in the World Hockey Association.\n- In the World Hockey Association, Pat Westrum played for the Minnesota Fighting Saints, Calgary Cowboys, and Birmingham Bulls.\n- As of 2009, the Minnesota Golden Gophers moved into the new TCF Bank Stadium on the University of Minnesota campus.\n- TCF Bank Stadium is an outdoor stadium on the campus of the University of Minnesota in Minneapolis, Minnesota, United States.\n- The Mill District is a neighborhood in Minneapolis, Minnesota, United States.\n- The Mill District is part of the larger Downtown East neighborhood.",
